["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0cae6-7e88-710c-8913-d70d29cb7b4c","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIG8a59970084e769b82ea85feff430468d77ad84a6a90736b7b68074ac7c27b326","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/pinned-startup-definition-bundle","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":5,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Context\n\nThe first service process needs an immutable definition registry, but dynamic registration and activation belong to a later lifecycle wave.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nA deterministic loader validates one definition tree, computes its SHA-256 digest from sorted relative paths and bytes, and refuses startup when the supplied expected digest does not name that validated bundle.\n\n## Implementation\n\nThe project loader now walks a definition tree in sorted relative-path order, validates every definition before admitting the bundle, hashes path and file bytes with SHA-256, and compares the resulting digest with an optional startup pin. Tests cover stable digests, content and path changes, invalid definitions, and expected-digest refusal.\n","relations":[{"serves":"vision:O2"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Validate and content-address the definitions a service process evaluates.","title":"Load one pinned startup definition bundle"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIG8a59970084e769b82ea85feff430468d77ad84a6a90736b7b68074ac7c27b326","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":5,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIG8a59970084e769b82ea85feff430468d77ad84a6a90736b7b68074ac7c27b326"]}]